## Why This Is Asked
Introduces a new angle: multi-sensor fusion with event cameras for high-dynamic scenes. Assesses architectural discipline and concrete trade-offs for low latency and on-device adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Event cameras and RGB fusion
- 3D voxel grids and lightweight transformers
- On-device 5-shot adaptation and object priors
- Temporal consistency and occlusion handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code: fuse RGB features with events, then predict pose and mask
function forward(rgbFrame, events, priors){
  const rgbFeat = rgbBackbone(rgbFrame);
  const evtFeat = eventBackbone(events);
  const fused = fuse3D(rgbFeat, evtFeat);
  const pose = poseHead(fused, priors);
  const mask = segHead(fused);
  return {pose, mask};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design synthetic data generation to cover unseen shapes with realistic event streams?
- What debugging metrics would help you diagnose latency vs. accuracy bottlenecks on edge hardware?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes on-device real-time hazard detection and 3D distance estimation under unseen categories, reflecting safety-critical constraints common in field deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time monocular depth on edge
- On-device meta-learning (5-shot)
- Synthetic+real data with domain randomization
- Temporal tracking and occlusion robustness
- Evaluation: detection, depth error, latency

## Code Example

```javascript
function forward(img, backbone, detectorHead, depthHead) {
  const feats = backbone.extract(img);
  const boxes = detectorHead.predict(feats);
  const depth = depthHead.predict(feats);
  return { boxes, depth };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ablate depth head accuracy vs. detector latency?
- What failure modes dominate in cluttered sites, and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked

